==Italian==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|ML.|it}} {{m|la|brūnus}} "brown, brunet" (whence also {{cog|es|bruno}}, {{cog|fr|brun}}), from {{etyl|frk|it}} *{{m|frk||brūn}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|it}} {{m|gem-pro|*brūnaz||brown}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|it}} {{m|ine-pro|*bher-||shining, brown}}. Akin to {{cog|odt|brūn}} "brown" ({{cog|nl|bruin}} "brown"), {{cog|goh|brūn}} "brown" ({{cog|de|braun}} "brown"), {{cog|ang|brūn}} "brown". More at {{l|en|brown}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{rhymes|it|uno}}

===Adjective===
